==English==

===Etymology===
Back-formation from {{m|en|upholsterer||tradesman who finishes furniture}}, from {{etyl|enm|en}} {{m|enm|upholdester}}, from {{m|enm|upholder||dealer in small goods}}, from {{m|enm|upholden||to repair, uphold}}; see also {{m|en|uphold}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|UK}} {{IPA|/əˈpɒl.stə(ɹ)/|/əˈpɐl.stə(ɹ)/|lang=en}}

===Verb===
{{en-verb}}

# To [[fit]] [[padding]], [[stuffing]], [[spring]]s, [[webbing]] and [[fabric]] [[covering]] to [[furniture]].

====Derived terms====
* [[reupholster]]
* [[upholsterer]]
* [[upholstering]]
* [[upholstery]]

